  "goodToKnow": "Der Pfosten is a post: der Zaunpfosten, der Türpfosten. In football, der Pfosten is the goalpost, and die Latte the crossbar: Der Ball ging an den Pfosten. Say both sounds of pf at once: PFOS-ten. It comes from Latin postis, like English post, and shows the High German sound shift that turned p into pf: Pfund (pound), Pfeffer (pepper), Pflanze (plant). The plural is the same."
